# Rails Database & Performance

## ActiveRecord Best Practices
- Use ActiveRecord effectively for database operations
- Use database indexing effectively
- Follow Rails naming conventions for models and associations

## Query Optimization
- Use eager loading to avoid N+1 queries
- Optimize database queries using `includes`, `joins`, or `select`
- Use `find_each` for large datasets instead of `find`

## Caching Strategies
- Implement fragment caching for expensive operations
- Use Russian Doll caching for nested data
- Cache frequently accessed data at appropriate levels

## Examples
```ruby
# Good: Eager loading to avoid N+1
users = User.includes(:posts, :comments)

# Good: Selective loading
User.select(:id, :name, :email).where(active: true)

# Good: Batch processing
User.find_each(batch_size: 1000) do |user|
  user.process_data
end

# Good: Fragment caching
cache("user_#{user.id}_#{user.updated_at.to_i}") do
  render user
end
```
